findings.detail:
Mutation run ev:ev-mv357tfj-0191a2c4, on scratch copies, the reviewed tree untouched:
- M0 control 41/41;
- M1, M3, M4, M5 killed as in iteration 1;
- the new M6 (grounding forced true), M7 (the old 'no digits' rule restored) and M8 (the probe validated without the text) are killed with 3, 2 and 3 of 26 red;
- M2, which removes `textNorm.includes(quote)` (extraction.js L385), now SURVIVES, 26/26 green. In iteration 1 it was killed.

The cause is the TR-D-1 fix: numeric fields are re-checked by validateExtraction, which rejects a quote that is not in the text (NOT_QUOTED). So L385 is the only guard for productType, material and deadline, and no test exercises it.

The code is correct today: my P3a shows material 'plastic' quoted 'plastic cups' stored unknown (ev:ev-mv35ahlo-01407cf7). But a regression would go unnoticed.

Carry item 1 lists all eleven deltas, with the three caveats in my wording:
- the UPLOAD_TIMEOUT branch is unreachable under the default 30 s requestTimeout;
- capabilities.deleteRequest is constant;
- the EXT-1 images are English-only.
The mapping is correct. The finding resolves when the verification report contains them.

resolvedFindings.resolution:
Resolved. extract-degraded.test.js L198, a named RS-03 test, has a stub provider reject ProviderError('PROVIDER_BUSY'). It asserts:
- 200 and exactly one call;
- degraded with errorCode PROVIDER_BUSY and every field unknown;
- model_spend is exactly [{actual 0, settled}], with no row reserved;
- the extractions row is {degraded 1, schema_ok 0, PROVIDER_BUSY}.
It passes in the d3 command and in npm test. My P1 gives the same result on HEAD: 200, degraded, PROVIDER_BUSY, spend {0, settled} (ev:ev-mv35098k-018beba3).
